## 1. Definitions

"Software" means the Kooboo software, including its source code, object code, documentation, configuration, tools, libraries, and other materials distributed by Kooboo under this License.

"Licensor" means Kooboo or the copyright holder of the Software.

"Authorized Partner" means an individual or organization that has been expressly authorized by the Licensor to access and use the Software under this License.

"Source Code" means the human-readable form of the Software, including source files, build scripts, configuration files, and other materials reasonably required to modify and build the Software.

"Derivative Work" means a modified version of the Software or a work based upon the Software.

## 2. Grant of License

Subject to the terms and conditions of this License, the Licensor grants each Authorized Partner a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to:

1. access and inspect the Source Code;
2. copy the Source Code internally for development and backup purposes;
3. modify the Source Code;
4. compile and build the Software and modified versions of the Software; and
5. use the Software and authorized Derivative Works for internal development and for developing, operating, and delivering websites, applications, and services for the Authorized Partner and its customers.

This license is granted only to the Authorized Partner and does not grant rights to the general public.

## 3. Partner Use

An Authorized Partner may use the Software and Derivative Works created under this License in connection with legitimate customer projects and services.

An Authorized Partner may deploy compiled versions of the Software as part of a website, application, hosting service, or other customer solution, provided that the Software is not distributed in a manner that gives an unauthorized person access to the Source Code.

An Authorized Partner may provide compiled Software to its customers when reasonably necessary to operate a customer project, but may not transfer the rights granted by this License to those customers.

## 4. Source Code Restrictions

The Source Code is proprietary and confidential intellectual property of the Licensor.

Except with prior written permission from the Licensor, an Authorized Partner must not:

1. publish the Source Code;
2. make the Source Code available on a public website, repository, package registry, file-sharing service, or similar service;
3. distribute the Source Code to any person or organization that is not an Authorized Partner;
4. sublicense, sell, lease, rent, or otherwise transfer the Source Code;
5. provide access to the Source Code through a public or shared development environment to unauthorized persons;
6. include the Source Code in another product or software distribution that is made available to unauthorized persons; or
7. disclose the Source Code or other proprietary materials of the Licensor except as expressly permitted by this License.

An Authorized Partner may make reasonable internal copies of the Source Code for its authorized developers and backup systems, provided that access remains limited to persons authorized by the Partner and bound by obligations at least as protective as those in this License.

## 5. Derivative Works

An Authorized Partner may create modifications and Derivative Works for its authorized business and customer projects.

The creation of a Derivative Work does not transfer ownership of the underlying Kooboo Software or Kooboo intellectual property to the Authorized Partner.

The Licensor retains all rights, title, and interest in the original Software and its underlying technology.

The Authorized Partner retains ownership of original code, designs, and other intellectual property independently created by the Partner, subject to the rights of the Licensor in the Kooboo Software incorporated into or required by such Derivative Work.

## 6. Redistribution

The Software and Source Code may not be redistributed except as expressly permitted by this License or by a separate written agreement with the Licensor.

In particular, an Authorized Partner may not distribute Kooboo or a Derivative Work as a general-purpose software product, framework, CMS, platform, or development system for use by third parties unless the Licensor has provided prior written authorization.

This restriction does not prevent an Authorized Partner from using Kooboo internally or deploying compiled Kooboo-based solutions for its customers as permitted under Section 3.

## 7. Competing Products

Without prior written permission from the Licensor, an Authorized Partner may not use the Source Code to create, market, or distribute a product whose primary purpose is to replace or compete directly with Kooboo as a general-purpose website development platform, CMS, web application platform, hosting platform, or substantially similar product.

This restriction does not prohibit an Authorized Partner from:

1. developing websites and applications for customers;
2. creating customer-specific customizations;
3. creating integrations, plugins, themes, templates, or extensions for authorized Kooboo projects; or
4. providing professional services based on Kooboo.

## 8. Branding and Trademarks

This License does not grant any right to use the Kooboo name, logo, trademarks, service marks, or other branding except as necessary to accurately identify the Software.

An Authorized Partner may state that a customer solution is built with or based on Kooboo, provided that such statement does not imply that the Partner is Kooboo or that Kooboo endorses the Partner.

## 9. Intellectual Property

The Software is proprietary software.

Except for the limited rights expressly granted by this License, the Licensor retains all copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, and other intellectual property rights in the Software.

No rights are granted by implication, estoppel, or otherwise.

## 10. Confidentiality

Where the Source Code is provided to an Authorized Partner under circumstances in which it is identified or reasonably understood to be confidential, the Authorized Partner must use reasonable measures to protect the Source Code from unauthorized access, disclosure, copying, or use.

The Authorized Partner must limit access to the Source Code to its employees, contractors, and developers who have a legitimate need to access it for purposes permitted by this License.

The Authorized Partner is responsible for ensuring that such persons are subject to confidentiality obligations appropriate to the nature of the Source Code.

## 11. Security and Vulnerabilities

An Authorized Partner may inspect the Source Code for security, compatibility, performance, debugging, and development purposes.

An Authorized Partner should promptly report significant security vulnerabilities discovered in the Software to the Licensor through the designated Kooboo security or partner communication channel.

Security research performed in good faith under an authorized partner relationship does not by itself constitute a violation of this License.

## 12. License Termination

This License automatically terminates if an Authorized Partner materially violates its terms.

Upon termination, the Authorized Partner must stop accessing and using the Source Code and must delete or return copies of the Source Code as reasonably requested by the Licensor, except where retention is required by applicable law.

Termination does not affect rights that accrued before termination, nor does it release either party from obligations that by their nature survive termination.

